the smoke test, slower. A completed-Q target (Gumbel AlphaZero) was tried next: with the warm net's sharp prior it barely moves off the prior. Run r2 uses expert iteration instead: the target is the search's chosen buy (most visits), the root gets no Dirichlet noise, exploration comes from drawing buys by visit counts in the first 6 turns and from the 30% of games against the GA. r2 reuses r1's warm start (iteration 0).","kind":"journal"}]